---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="Website privacy notice"
  description="What this website does and does not collect. No accounts, no forms, no cookies, no analytics, no tracking."
  path="/website-privacy"
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="page-head-stack">
        <p class="eyebrow">Website privacy notice</p>
        <h1 class="display display--page">This website collects nothing.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          A short notice about this site specifically. It is separate from the Discord bot's
          Privacy Policy, which does not cover the website.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--flush">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="notice notice--neutral" role="note" style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <span class="status status--planned">Scope</span>
        <p class="notice-body">
          This notice covers <strong>nextstepstudios website</strong> pages only. The
          <a class="text-link" href="/policies/bot/privacy">Discord Bot Privacy Policy</a>
          covers the bot, and is a separate document.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-layout" style="grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);">
        <article class="prose">
          <h2>What this site does not do</h2>
          <p>The website has no accounts, no sign-in, no contact forms, no comment sections, no downloads that require details, and no newsletter. Specifically, it does not use:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>cookies or similar storage technologies;</li>
            <li>analytics, statistics or audience-measurement services;</li>
            <li>advertising, advertising pixels or affiliate tracking;</li>
            <li>session recording, heatmaps or fingerprinting;</li>
            <li>third-party embeds, widgets or social plugins;</li>
            <li>third-party fonts, scripts or content delivery networks.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            The site is built as static pages and the fonts are served from the site itself.
            No information is stored in your browser by this site.
          </p>

          <h2>Hosting and technical logs</h2>
          <p>
            The site is served by a hosting provider, which necessarily processes network
            requests to deliver pages. Like most hosting, this may involve standard request
            logs — such as the requesting IP address, the browser's user agent, the requested
            page, and a timestamp — kept by the provider for delivery, security and
            troubleshooting.
          </p>
          <p>
            These logs are not used by the Studio for profiling, advertising or tracking, and
            this site does not combine them with any other information. The exact logging and
            retention behaviour of the hosting provider is set by that provider rather than by
            this website, and it is not described in more detail here than has been confirmed.
          </p>

          <h2>Email</h2>
          <p>
            If you email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>, the
            Studio receives your email address, the contents of your message, and anything you
            choose to attach, and uses them to read and answer your message. Email is handled
            by the third-party email provider that hosts that mailbox.
          </p>
          <p>
            Messages are kept as long as needed to deal with the matter they concern. No
            specific retention period is stated here, because none has been fixed and verified
            — stating one would be inventing it.
          </p>

          <h2>What this notice does not claim</h2>
          <p>
            This notice describes what the website actually does. It is not a legal opinion
            and does not claim compliance with any particular law or regulation. If the site
            later adds a feature that collects information — a form, analytics, an account
            system — this notice will be rewritten before that feature goes live.
          </p>

          <h2>Changes</h2>
          <p>
            This notice is updated when the website's behaviour changes. It carries no version
            history yet because it is the first version.
          </p>

          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Questions about this notice, or about the website, go to
            <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>. Requests
            concerning information held by the Discord bot are handled through the same
            address — see <a href="/contact#privacy-requests">privacy requests</a>.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
